<section id="A6" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix F </span>Additional Transfer Results</h2>

<div id="A6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_label ltx_ref_self"></span> shows the full transfer learning results described in <a href="#S4" title="4 Other Applications ‣ What Has a Foundation Model Found?Using Inductive Bias to Probe for World Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A7" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix G </span>Next Token Performance</h2>

<div id="A7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><a href="#A7.T6" title="In Appendix G Next Token Performance ‣ What Has a Foundation Model Found?Using Inductive Bias to Probe for World Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> shows results for the next-token test <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib43" title="" class="ltx_ref">Toshniwal et al., 2022</a>; <a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">Li et al., 2023</a>)</cite> for the pre-trained models on the lattice and Othello models. It measures the share of top model predictions that are true for the underlying state. All models learn good next token predictions that appear to obey state.</p>
</div>
<div id="A7.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><a href="#A7.T7" title="In Appendix G Next Token Performance ‣ What Has a Foundation Model Found?Using Inductive Bias to Probe for World Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> shows results for physics.
Across 200 held-out trajectories, we autoregressively generate
the model’s predicted trajectory given the first 50 steps.
Then, we compute the MSE of the predicted trajectory, <math id="A7.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1,5,10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1,5,10</annotation></semantics></math> steps from the 50<sup id="A7.p2.1.1" class="ltx_sup"><span id="A7.p2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">th</span></sup> step.
We include the MSE of a baseline that always predicts the most recent timestep.</p>
</div>
